Keep the completion predicate under the existing task mutex.

waiting, tasks_running, paused and tasks are plain state protected by
tasks_mutex. Reading them after unlock races with wait(), queueing, pause
and other workers. Notification while holding the mutex is valid; the
following condition-variable wait releases it normally.

Accepted by chronium, 2026-10-24. This upstream-derived patch retains MIT
terms. Remove it when the selected upstream revision contains the fix.

diff --git a/include/BS_thread_pool.hpp b/include/BS_thread_pool.hpp
--- a/include/BS_thread_pool.hpp
+++ b/include/BS_thread_pool.hpp
@@ -913,10 +913,8 @@ private:
         while (true)
         {
             --tasks_running;
-            tasks_lock.unlock();
             if (waiting && (tasks_running == 0) && BS_THREAD_POOL_PAUSED_OR_EMPTY)
                 tasks_done_cv.notify_all();
-            tasks_lock.lock();
             task_available_cv.wait(tasks_lock,
